  "security_implications": "The signal message_length_d directly influences the HMAC length field and therefore the integrity of the authentication tag. Incorrect handling of message_length—whether through accidental zeroing when hash_start collides with CSR writes, silent integer wraparound, or misaligned write handshakes—can allow an attacker to forge valid HMAC tags for modified messages. The block also gates CSR writes behind cfg_block, which may affect debug or lifecycle-controlled length programming; a mismatch here could create a side‑channel for adversarial length manipulation.",
